Job Description
We are currently running an ongoing project with our partners for the United Nations and we are in need of a senior SAP Business Analyst/Functional Specialist for Nigeria.
Tasks
Support the blueprint, build, realization, production support and continual improvement stages of the Umoja solution in specific functional areas (financial accounting, financial management, budget formulation, logistics & supply chain management, or human capital management) with emphasis on a specific set of modules and tools, as per the specific statement of work;
Work closely with the Solution Architecture team and business analysts from other functional areas, to ensure alignment with the Organization's application architecture;
Interact with stakeholders at various levels of the Organization, from technical teams to IT and senior business executives to business experts;
Support the implementation of business processes in tbe specific functional area(s);
Based on approved business requirements, work with end users and Solution Architects to develop and/or update functional specification documents for configuration as well as FRICEW objects;
Analyse complex business problems to be solved with the SAP solution and assist end users and process experts in articulating business requirements;
Update and review configuration documentation to ensure it meets project standards, and has effectively captured business requirements;
Conduct knowledge transfer on the specific area of expertise. Act as a Trainer, as part of knowledge transfer, to conduct training of trainers as well develop business process experts;
Develop, review and refine the corresponding test scripts/use cases for all phases of testing;
Assist with executing and validating testing results, to ensure that the system is compliant with business process requirements, and supports defect resolution;
Provide technical support in the use of methods and tools for data cleansing and migration;
Provide support in solution cut-over planning, as well as in its deployment;
Write and maintain process design documents, functional specifications, and business design documents for new and/or modified business requirements;
Prepare substantive content required for the development of user documentation, learning materials, instructions, and procedures. Where required, prepares the final documentation, following established United Nations Secretariat standards, including presentations;
Provide Tier 3 production support in the corresponding functional area of expertise;
Supervise the work of junior business analysts, as well as performing quality assurance and providing coaching and knowledge transfer.
Required Skills
A minimum of 5 years of SAP functional experience with select processes in a specific functional area, including analysis, specification development, configuration, testing, end user support;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
Experience with test script planning, development/execution/defect resolution processes;
Area of Expertise: SAP business analysis, supervisory skills, SAP configuration in a specific module(s) and/or product(s) as per statement of work, writing technical documentation, delivering end-user presentations.
